 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Sessions live in signed cookies, implemented by `sign` and `verify` in `larder/sessions.py`. The cookie contains
+base64-encoded JSON with the member id (`member`) and expiry (`expires`), followed by an HMAC-SHA256 signature.
+The contents are encoded, not encrypted. Verification checks the signature and expiry before returning the member
+id; a signature mismatch or a past expiry returns `None`. There is no session table or per-request session query.
+
+## Signing key and logout
+
+`LARDER_SESSION_KEY` comes from the deploy secrets and must be the same on every web server. The module reads it
+at import time; if it is absent, the code falls back to `dev-only`, a development default. Deployments using the
+same key preserve sessions, including requests served by another server.
+
+There is no way to revoke one member's session on the server before its cookie expires. Rotating the shared key
+invalidates all existing session cookies and logs everyone out, so rotate it only between pickups. Ensure all web
+servers load the new key together.
 
